  "body": "Found in the review read of PR #3632 (#3627). From a read of the code; no test shows it yet.\n\n**Where:** `crates/motion/src/finishing3d/rings.rs`, about lines 338 and 488 (at `1e7800a9e`). The hop between two rings of one level is lifted to the ring level, so it does not go down. The move across is made at the retract height and is not checked against the model.\n\n**Case:** two waterline rings at z 5 around two bosses with their top at z 10, and a retract height of 7. The chord between the rings can cross a boss.\n\n**Expected today:** the verifier finds the rapid in the part and holds the post. So this is a refused program with a cause that the user must find, not a silent gouge. The first step is a test that shows the moves and the finding.\n\n**Wanted:** the same rule as #3627 for this hop: the move across stays at its height only when that height is at or above the model top, or when `straight_ok` clears it. If not, the hop goes to the clearance height. Pin the two-boss case and the normal case (no change).\n",
